"10"]],["DIV",{"class":"ei-table-wrap"},["TABLE",{},["CAPTION",{"class":"ei-small","style":"text-align: left;"},"Founders compared with the generation you are viewing"],["THEAD",{},["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Trait"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Founders"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Viewed"]]],["TBODY",{},["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"row"},"Coat lightness"],["TD",{},"52%"],["TD",{},"52%"]],["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"row"},"Insulation"],["TD",{},"52%"],["TD",{},"52%"]],["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"row"},"Leg length"],["TD",{},"45%"],["TD",{},"45%"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Generation table"],["DIV",{"class":"ei-table-wrap","style":"max-height: 250px;"},["TABLE",{},["THEAD",{},["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Generation"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Habitat"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Population"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Insulation"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Coat"],["TH",{"scope":"col"},"Legs"]]],["TBODY",{},["TR",{},["TH",{"scope":"row"},"0"],["TD",{},"Sunlit meadow"],["TD",{},"36"],["TD",{},"52%"],["TD",{},"52%"],["TD",{},"45%"]]]]]],["P",{"class":"ei-small"},"Dashed vertical markers show habitat changes. These are population averages, not upgrades to individual creatures. A single run mixes selection and chance; repeat with fresh seeds to look for a pattern."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Save finding to journal"]]],["DIV",{"class":"ei-callout"},["STRONG",{},"Watch populations change. "],"Each spriglet keeps the genes it was born with. Evolution appears across generations as different parents leave offspring. Walking and hopping are decorative; survival is calculated once per generation."],["DETAILS",{"class":"ei-card ei-stack"},["SUMMARY",{},"Your expedition log"],["DIV",{"class":"ei-log"},["DIV",{"class":"ei-log-entry"},["B",{},"G0"],["DIV",{},["STRONG",{},"A population full of possibilities"],["SMALL",{},"36 founders. Three inherited traits. No two gene combinations are the same."]]]]]]]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"ei-card","style":"margin-top: 17px;"},["SUMMARY",{},"How this world works · teacher notes"],["DIV",{"class":"ei-stack"},["P",{"class":"ei-small"},"Spriglets are fictional organisms in a simplified population-genetics model. Three independent diploid loci control continuous traits; one allele per locus comes from each of two randomly sampled surviving parents. The trait is the average of its two alleles. Survival depends on habitat, coat camouflage, insulation, leg length, food, and chance. Longer legs aid escape but cost energy. Mutations happen during inheritance, with no knowledge of the environment."],["P",{"class":"ei-small"},"Generations do not overlap. At least two survivors are needed to breed. The next population has 2.65 offspring per survivor, rounded down and capped at 60. Carrying capacity, trait effects, and mutation rates are teaching choices, not measurements. The model omits migration, linkage, dominance, learned behavior, age structure, and reproductive isolation. It does not simulate the full evolutionary process or demonstrate speciation."],["P",{"class":"ei-small"},"Try a 10-minute investigation: inspect two founders; predict the effect of a long winter; hold that habitat for five generations; compare allele pairs in parents and offspring. Repeat with a fresh seed. Then disable trait-based survival to investigate drift. A single run cannot separate all causes of change."],["P",{"class":"ei-small"},"The scenery draws inspiration from Galápagos lava shores, arid scrub, and greener highlands. This is a fictional island, not a geographic replica. Winter is an experimental climate, not a Galápagos season. Terrain, plants, water, and scenic viewpoints are visual context: all spriglets experience the selected habitat, regardless of position. This tool follows inherited traits across generations; the Ecosystem tool explores interactions between species and resources."],["A",{"href":"https://www.galapagos.org/about_galapagos/biodiversity/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"ei-small"},"Landscape inspiration: Galápagos Conservancy — habitats"],["A",{"href":"https://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolution-101/mechanisms-the-processes-of-evolution/mutations/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"ei-small"},"Science reference: UC Berkeley Understanding Evolution — mutations"]]],["DIV",{"style":"margin-top: 17px;"},["DIV",{"class":"evolab-no-print bg-white border-2 border-slate-300 rounded-xl p-4"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-start justify-between gap-2 mb-2"},["DIV",{},["LABEL",{"for":"evolab-note-livingIsland","class":"block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700"},"📝 My field note"],["P",{"class":"text-sm text-slate-700 mt-1"},"What changed in your population? Use a before-and-after number, explain inheritance and survival, and name one limit of this model."]],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-label":"Read this aloud","title":"Read this aloud","class":"evolab-no-print inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full w-8 h-8 text-base transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 bg-slate-100 hover:bg-slate-200 text-slate-700 focus:ring-slate-400"},"🔊"]],["DIV",{"role":"group","aria-label":"Note shape","class":"mb-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","class":"rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold bg-slate-800 text-white"},"Free note"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","class":"rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-200"},"Claim · Evidence · Reasoning"]],["TEXTAREA",{"__playwright_value_":"","id":"evolab-note-livingIsland","rows":"3","maxlength":"2000","placeholder":"Write one or two sentences in your own words…","class":"w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-500 p-2 text-sm text-slate-900 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-400"}],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-slate-600"},"0 / 2000"],["DIV",{"class":"flex 